"comparison": "Both JPMorgan Chase and Bank of America define Total Loss-Absorbing Capacity (TLAC) as comprising Tier 1 capital and eligible long-term debt. However, JPMorgan's disclosure focuses on presenting the specific eligible external TLAC and LTD amounts and their percentages of Risk-Weighted Assets (RWA) and leverage exposure, while Bank of America's disclosure defines the composition of TLAC and the requirement to maintain ratios in excess of minimums plus buffers to avoid restrictions on capital distributions and discretionary bonus payments.",
