"comparison": "Both companies disclose their Long-Term Debt (LTD) regulatory minimums. JPMorgan presents a table of eligible LTD amounts as a percentage of total RWA and leverage exposure, incorporating CECL transition provisions. Bank of America explicitly states that its long-term debt RWA regulatory minimum increased from 8.5% to 9.0% effective January 1, 2024, due to a 50 bps increase in the G-SIB surcharge, while maintaining a 4.5% leverage exposure minimum, providing the specific regulatory drivers for the minimums that JPMorgan reports on but does not explicitly break down in this specific excerpt.",
