"comparison": "Both JPMorgan Chase and Goldman Sachs define the components of TLAC and eligible long-term debt. JPMorgan refers to eligible external TLAC and eligible LTD amounts. Goldman Sachs explicitly states that TLAC includes common and preferred stock and eligible long-term debt issued by Group Inc., defined as unsecured debt with at least one year maturity, and that external long-term debt consists of eligible long-term debt subject to a haircut if due between one and two years, providing the structural definition of the 'eligible' amounts JPMorgan reports.",
