"comparison": "Both JPMorgan Chase and Morgan Stanley are covered BHCs/GSIBs required to maintain minimum external TLAC and LTD. JPMorgan presents its eligible external TLAC and LTD amounts as a percentage of total RWA and leverage exposure. Morgan Stanley specifies the minimum requirements: external TLAC must be the greater of 18% of total RWA or 7.5% of total leverage exposure, and external LTD must be the greater of total RWA multiplied by 6% plus G-SIB surcharge or 4.5% of total leverage exposure, providing the specific regulatory thresholds that underpin the ratios JPMorgan reports.",
